Finally, long overdue, version 2.1.0 has now been released, tagged on the
master branch.

Pending changes to jalv to set parameters that not described in a loaded .ttl
file to their default values, I went ahead and implemented some changes that do
not require new parameters. Originally I hadn’t planned on implementing the
oscillator shape feature until later, not considering it important enough, and
fearing that it would a bit of a rabbit hole - which it was. Especially the
sawtooth shape took some time, and although it’s not as useful as the
triangle-sawtoth morph, I wanted to include it as it is a feature of the
original MiMi-a.

There are essentially two changes in this release:

- The Pulsewidth parameter has been renamed to Shape, since it now affects the
  triangle and sawtooth oscillator waveshapes. For the triangle, the waveform
  can be morphed from a classic triangle (parameter value 0) to sawtooth
  (parameter value 10). For the sawtooth, it can be morphed from a classic
  sawtooth (parameter value 0) to a very spiky sawtooth (parameter value 10).
- Polyphonic aftertouch is now supported. There is no parameter to select
  betwen channel and polyphonic aftertouch, the plugin simply reacts to
  whatever arrives in terms of MIDI messages.

There is also a bunch of new presets, a lot of them attempting to showcase the new shape parameter. The presets whose names start with “Trapezoid” morph the triangle waveform between sawtooth and (near) triangle, in effect emulating a low pass filter of sorts with the shape parameter.

As usual, a companion version 2.1.0z has been tagged on the Zynthian branch, which supports the graphic envelope feature in the Zynthian UI.
